      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We start with the given equation:\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 = 10x - 6y - 34.\n\\]\nRewrite the equation by completing the square for both \\(x\\) and \\(y\\):\n\\[\nx^2 - 10x + y^2 + 6y = -34,\n\\]\n\\[\n(x^2 - 10x + 25) + (y^2 + 6y + 9) = -34 + 25 + 9,\n\\]\n\\[\n(x - 5)^2 + (y + 3)^2 = 0.\n\\]\nSince the sum of two squares is zero, each square must individually be zero. Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n(x - 5)^2 = 0 \\implies x = 5,\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n(y + 3)^2 = 0 \\implies y = -3.\n\\]\nThus, the values of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are \\(x = 5\\) and \\(y = -3\\). Therefore, the sum \\(x + y\\) is:\n\\[\nx + y = 5 + (-3) = 2.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
